---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/site";
import { buildMeta, organizationSchema } from "../lib/seo";
import { appStoreUrl } from "../lib/analytics";

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: "Harmless Apps | Low-stimulation and educational apps for kids",
  description:
    "Independent kids app reviews focused on low stimulation, educational value, offline use, and products parents can feel confident handing to their children.",
  pathname: "/"
});
---

<BaseLayout {...meta} schemas={[organizationSchema()]}>
  <section class="mission-hero">
    <div class="shell mission-grid">
      <div class="mission-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Independent app lab · built by a mom</p>
        <h1>Apps you’re <mark>not scared</mark> to hand to your kids.</h1>
        <p class="mission-lede">
          Harmless Apps finds and builds low-stimulation, educational digital
          products that respect a child’s attention—and a parent’s trust.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/best-low-stimulation-apps-for-toddlers/">Explore the ratings</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={siteConfig.productPath}>Meet Denny’s Maze</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="mission-note" aria-label="The Harmless Apps standard">
        <p class="micro-label">What I look for</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span>01</span>Calmer visual and audio design</li>
          <li><span>02</span>Real learning and child agency</li>
          <li><span>03</span>Reliable offline play</li>
          <li><span>04</span>Respectful commercial design</li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="why-section">
    <div class="shell why-grid">
      <p class="section-index">01 / Mission</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Finding the good ones shouldn’t be this hard.</h2>
        <p>
          The App Store is full of products labeled educational. That does not
          tell you whether an app is noisy, manipulative, shallow, impossible
          to use offline, or genuinely useful for a young child.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="mission-link" href="/ratings/apps/">I test those things directly</a>,
          using the same question I ask as a parent: would I feel comfortable
          giving this to my own child?
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="routes-section" aria-labelledby="start-here">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-index">02 / Start here</p>
        <h2 id="start-here">Three ways into the work.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="route-grid">
        <article class="route-card route-denny">
          <div class="route-number">01</div>
          <div class="route-art">
            <img src="/images/app-icons/dennys-maze.jpg" alt="Denny's Maze app icon" width="512" height="512" loading="eager" />
          </div>
          <div class="route-copy">
            <p class="micro-label">Made here</p>
            <h3>Denny’s Maze</h3>
            <p>
              I built the product I wanted first: a quiet maze-book experience
              with no ads, no timers, and no flashing reward loops. It is the
              app I can confidently give to my own child.
            </p>
            <div class="route-actions">
              <a class="text-link" href={siteConfig.productPath}>See the app <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              <a class="button lime app-store-link" href={appStoreUrl("website_home_hero")} data-app-store-cta="product-card" data-app-store-campaign="website_home_hero">View on the App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <a class="route-card route-rating" href="/best-low-stimulation-apps-for-toddlers/">
          <div class="route-number">02</div>
          <p class="micro-label">Independent testing</p>
          <h3>Low-stimulation ratings</h3>
          <p>
            Compare visual motion, audio intensity, reward loops, interruptions,
            child agency, and learning value across popular kids apps.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">See the comparison <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
        </a>

        <a class="route-card route-offline" href="/offline-toddler-apps/">
          <div class="route-number">03</div>
          <p class="micro-label">Travel-tested</p>
          <h3>Offline app ratings</h3>
          <p>
            See what actually works after Wi-Fi disappears, what needs setup,
            and what gives a child enough to do on a real trip.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">See the offline tests <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="standards-section">
    <div class="shell standards-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">03 / The standard</p>
        <h2>Educational is more than a label.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="standards-list">
        <div><span>Skill demand</span><p>What does the child actually have to think about or do?</p></div>
        <div><span>Agency</span><p>Does the child make meaningful choices, or mostly follow prompts?</p></div>
        <div><span>Depth</span><p>Does the experience develop, or repeat the same shallow interaction?</p></div>
        <div><span>Transfer</span><p>Could the learning matter beyond this one app?</p></div>
      </div>
      <a class="button lime" href="/ratings/methodology/">Read the methodology</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="founder-section">
    <div class="shell founder-grid">
      <div class="founder-label">
        <span class="lime-rule"></span>
        <p class="micro-label">Why this exists</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>I wanted better apps for my own child.</h2>
        <p>
          I spent 13 years building apps designed to hold attention. After
          becoming a mom, I wanted to use those skills differently. Denny’s Maze
          came first. Then I started testing the rest of the market—with the same
          standards I use for my own product and my own child.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link light" href="/blog/i-spent-13-years-making-apps-impossible-to-put-down/">Read my story <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .mission-hero { padding: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem) 0 clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); overflow: hidden; }
  .mission-grid { display: grid; gap: 4rem; align-items: end; }
  .mission-grid > * { min-width: 0; }
  .mission-copy { max-width: 58rem; }
  .mission-copy .eyebrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.8rem; }
  .mission-copy .eyebrow span, .lime-rule { width: 5rem; height: 0.45rem; background: var(--lime); display: inline-block; }
  .mission-copy h1 { max-width: 14ch; margin-top: 1.5rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .mission-copy mark { background: var(--lime); color: inherit; padding: 0 0.08em; -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; box-decoration-break: clone; }
  .mission-lede { max-width: 42rem; margin: 2rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 1.65rem); line-height: 1.45; }
  .mission-note { padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .mission-note ol { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }
  .mission-note li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-weight: 650; }
  .mission-note li span { color: var(--blue); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem; }
  .micro-label, .section-index { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .section-index { color: var(--muted); }
  .why-section { padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0; background: var(--navy); color: white; }
  .why-grid { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  .why-section .section-index { color: var(--lime); }
  .why-section h2 { max-width: 13ch; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .why-section p:not(.section-index) { max-width: 47rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,.82); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .mission-link { color: var(--navy); background: var(--lime); padding: 0.08em 0.18em; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; box-decoration-break: clone; }
  .mission-link:hover { background: var(--pale-lime); }
  .routes-section { padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0; }
  .section-heading { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .section-heading h2 { max-width: 15ch; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .route-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .route-card { position: relative; min-height: 24rem; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; overflow: hidden; }
  .route-card h3 { max-width: 14ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .route-card p:not(.micro-label) { max-width: 36rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .route-number { position: absolute; top: 1.4rem; right: 1.4rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); }
  .route-denny { display: grid; gap: 1rem; background: white; }
  .route-art { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 16rem; aspect-ratio: 1; padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem); background: white; }
  .route-art img { display: block; width: min(100%, 15rem); height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1; object-fit: contain; border-radius: 22%; box-shadow: none; }
  .route-copy { padding: 0.5rem 0; }
  .route-rating { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: flex-end; background: var(--navy); color: white; }
  .route-rating p:not(.micro-label), .route-rating .route-number { color: rgba(255,255,255,.68); }
  .route-rating .micro-label { color: var(--lime); }
  .route-offline { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: flex-end; background: var(--lime); }
  .route-offline p:not(.micro-label) { color: rgba(18,24,51,.72); }
  .route-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .route-actions .app-store-link { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .text-link { display: inline-flex; gap: 0.55rem; align-items: center; margin-top: auto; padding-top: 1.5rem; color: inherit; font-weight: 750; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor; }
  .standards-section { padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .standards-grid { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; }
  .standards-grid h2 { max-width: 13ch; margin-top: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .standards-list > div { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 1.15rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .standards-list span { font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .standards-list p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .standards-grid .button { justify-self: start; }
  .founder-section { padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0; background: var(--navy); color: white; }
  .founder-grid { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  .founder-label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; color: var(--lime); }
  .founder-section h2 { max-width: 14ch; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .founder-section p:not(.micro-label) { max-width: 47rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,.72); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .text-link.light { color: white; }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .mission-copy .eyebrow { align-items: flex-start; }
    .mission-copy .eyebrow span { width: 3rem; flex: 0 0 3rem; margin-top: 0.35rem; }
    .mission-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 11vw, 3.35rem); }
    .mission-copy .hero-actions { display: grid; }
    .mission-copy .hero-actions .button { width: 100%; }
    .route-card h3 { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .mission-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(18rem, .8fr); }
    .why-grid, .founder-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, .45fr) minmax(0, 1.55fr); }
    .section-heading { grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, .45fr) minmax(0, 1.55fr); }
    .route-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .route-denny { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; padding: 0; }
    .route-copy { padding: 3rem; align-self: center; }
    .standards-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); }
    .standards-grid .button { grid-column: 2; }
  }
</style>
